Package: bst260projhelp
Title: Extract Tables and Verify Bibliographic Integrity from PDF Reports
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("Vincent", "Carey", email = "stvjc@channing.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for two recurring tasks when working with long PDF reports
    (such as government and NGO surveillance summaries): (1) recovering
    tabular data from PDF pages via either simple line-based parsing or
    coordinate-based word clustering, and (2) recovering a document's
    bibliography -- parsing its reference list, linking in-text citations
    to reference-list entries, and exporting the result as BibTeX or
    CSL-JSON for downstream citation-integrity checks. Includes worked
    examples on a RAND report on gun policy research and a CDC waterborne
    disease surveillance report.
